is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: srv1
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the HTTP web service on SRV1 (10.5.0.4) is down; DNS on SRV1 is up and authoritative.

Mechanism: Users see “not found” when browsing jeremysitlab.com because the web server on SRV1 is not accepting connections. Name resolution works and returns 10.5.0.4, but TCP/80 on that host refuses connections, so browsers fail to load pages.

Localization: On SRV1 (eth0, 10.5.0.4/24), named (BIND) is listening on 10.5.0.4:53 and serving the zone jeremysitlab.com authoritatively (nslookup returns A records; recursion not available as expected). However, there is no listener on TCP/80 and no nginx/apache/httpd process. From a client (pc1), curl to http://srv1.jeremysitlab.com/ fails with “connect to 10.5.0.4 port 80: Connection refused,” confirming no web service. Netstat/ss on SRV1 shows only :53 listeners, further confirming HTTP is down.

Root cause: The web server daemon on SRV1 is not running (stopped/crashed or not installed), while DNS is operating normally.

Corrective fix: Start or (if necessary) install and enable the HTTP service on SRV1. For example, if using Apache: systemctl start apache2 && systemctl enable apache2; if using Nginx: systemctl start nginx && systemctl enable nginx. Verify it listens on 0.0.0.0:80 (ss -ltnp) and that /var/www/html serves content. No network or DNS changes are required; SRV1’s DNS (bind/named) is healthy. After restoration, re-test with curl http://jeremysitlab.com/ from a client to confirm HTTP 200/expected content. === END ===